_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 17
---
order: 17
---
short_label: V.17
---
statement: If magnitudes are proportional taken jointly, then they are also proportional taken separately.
---
proof:

Let *AB, BE, CD,* and *DF* be magnitudes proportional taken jointly, so that *AB* is to *BE* as *CD* is to *DF.* [!just V.Def.14]

I say that they are also proportional taken separately, that is, *AE* is to *EB* as *CF* is to *DF.* [!just V.Def.15]

Take equimultiples *GH, HK, LM,* and *MN* of *AE, EB, CF,* and *FD,* and take other, arbitrary, equimultiples, *KO* and *NP* of *EB* and *FD.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="470" height="120" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="V.17 diagram" src="propV17.gif"/></noscript>
